hey what is up guys I'm Kay Bhd here and  first of all yes there is a ps4 in the  house a lot of people are asking so  thumbs up if you actually want to see me  cover that let me know but this is a  first look at a curved smartphone this  is the Samsung Galaxy round actually  personally a bit more excited for the LG  G flex because that seems way more  unique than this Galaxy round is as a  product but there's still a lot of  interesting things that we can look at  in the first available curved display  smartphone so not any further ado let's  go and take a full look so at first  glance the galaxy round actually doesn't  come off as all that crazy of a product  it seems like just your typical Samsung  smartphone in fact it looks like it's  older brother the Galaxy Note 3 quite a  bit it has that same 5.7 inch 1080p  AMOLED display on the front the same  faux leather stitching on the back  though a slightly different more brown  leather color and it really actually  shares a lot of the specs and hardware  with the Galaxy Note 3 like the  excellent 13 megapixel camera and the  flash you know what that's exactly what  this is a curved display galaxy note 3  I'll have my full galaxy note 3 review  right below that like button if you want  a refresher on how awesome that device  is but because this galaxy round is  curved it makes a few trade-offs and it  comes back at those with a few bonus  features so here are all the differences  between the galaxy round and the galaxy  note 3 number one is the backing the  back of the Galaxy Note 3 is obviously  flat and of course has that leatherette  stitching pattern we all know on the  back the back of the galaxy round is a  little different when you take it off  it's actually a bit more rigid more bent  into the curved shape of the round to  fit the back of the phone now it's  obviously still plastic it's not some  crazy new material or anything like that  it's very familiar but it's a little bit  more rigid because it's bent into that  shape now of course when you remove the  back you reveal numbers 2 &amp; 3 that are  different the speaker and the battery  now the speaker is obviously it's just a  little bit bigger it fires out the back  of the phone instead of the bottom like  on the note 3 but the battery is a  bigger difference so it's actually a bit  smaller in fact it's a totally different  shape and it's shrunk down from 32  hundred milli amp hours to a tall  slender 2800 milliamp hours this is  because the phone is curved so you know  there's less room to fit a back  in the phone when you curve it like this  now even though that's only a relatively  small difference it's a 400 milliamp  hour difference now I still get all day  battery out of this phone with a twenty  eight hundred million power battery but  Samsung want the extra mile here to  bring us to number four which is the  included accessories Samsung bundles an  extra battery and a second battery  charger like an external battery charger  for this galaxy round that's why the box  looks so much bigger than the galaxy  note 3 box you get all these extra  accessories with it so this battery  charger it charges your secondary  battery by USB 2.0 you still can charge  the phones via a USB 3.0 but I mean  that's nice that's a nice touch I'm glad  they threw an extra battery in there now  another difference in accessories is the  obvious lack of an S Pen in the galaxy  round it's not part of the note line  technically but I mean it's also curved  so there's really not that much space to  put an S Pen so the next difference is  by the numbers the galaxy round is  technically a little bit thinner and a  little bit lighter than the note 3 but  not really by all that much it's it's  about more of the way it feels in the  hand it just feels slightly more compact  but that's not because of the thinness  and the lightness that's because of the  biggest difference between these phones  the display now again on paper it starts  off very similar they both have a 5.7  inch 1080p AMOLED display and they're  both gorgeous and very vivid and very  bright but the slight curve radius on  the round makes it stick out quite  literally the shape is actually really  slight very subtle almost seems like the  middle of the phone is still flat while  only the sides curve up a bit it's a  really interesting shape and after using  a phone for more than a week I'll tell  you what don't judge me I totally got  used to it you don't really notice the  curve when looking at the actual images  on the display after about a day or so  but you can still always feel the curve  with your finger and it feels nice now  this curve radius does a few things one  I think it actually improves the extreme  viewing angles by a tiny bit which isn't  particularly useful for a lot of people  but hey that's a thing that I noticed  and it also creates some weird  reflections to this day that distracted  me a little bit when I look over on my  desk and I see this warped reflection  looking back and make kind of strange  and number three it actually shrinks the  amount of stretching you have to do to  use this phone with smaller hands and I  feel like it made a significant  especially noticeable when typing typing  on this keyboard in the display is way  easier on the round than it is on any  other similar size splat smartphone now  the galaxy round has pretty much  identical software to the galaxy note 3  in the Korean market but Samsung threw  in this neat software feature called the  roll effect so basically when the phone  is sitting with the screen off you can  roll it onto its side and get a quick  glance at your notifications and the  time and the battery status it's  sensitive to the accelerometer too so  you can literally just lift it up  sideways and get the same effect  unfortunately it's hard for the phone to  determine when this is being done on  purpose so there's like a really solid  delay between you tilting the phone and  showing the preview and that sucks  because I think it's going to prevent  people from using it especially when it  doesn't take much more effort to just  simply tap the power button and check  your notifications the regular way but  besides all the Samsung gimmicky stuff I  am seriously a fan of using the galaxy  round I really enjoyed it I got judged  so hard on Google+ and Twitter for  admitting that I really am into this I'm  excited to see what other form factors  sort of emerge that we see in 2014 that  aren't the usual slab form factor you  should be too but yeah at the end of the  day when it comes down to it the curve  is quite subtle the actual curve radius  is a lot smaller than a lot of people  have made it out to look and a lot of  the images but it essentially feels a  lot like a slightly more compact galaxy  note 3 so I guess that makes it a pretty  well-rounded device in other words you  leave your comments down below and more  importantly I want to hear which one you  think you would like better the LG G  flex which curves vertically or the  galaxy round which curves horizontally  let me know in a comment below and I'll  be sure to get my coverage of the G flex  up soon and if you guys want the ps4  thanks for watching guys basically
 

